WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.240
Can you help me check the PowerPoint

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.240
I made for the presentation? 

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.270
So you are using visual aids in your presentation? 

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:10.290
That’s good

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.240
Do you know people absorb 80 percent

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.180 
of the information they learn through seeing?

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.190
That’s why visual aids are 

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.150
so effective in presentations

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.260
I’ve included graphs and charts in my slides

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:30.040 
Charts, such as pie charts and bar charts

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.160
show the percentage and the breakdown of the data

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.000
What other visual aids can I use?

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.150
There are tables and figures

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.010 
which we find more often on printed materials

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.290 
We can also use diagrams, such as flow charts

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:50.140
to explain a process or procedure

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.100
The use of video and images can also

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.000 
successfully communicate ideas 

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.170
and attract people’s attention, right? 

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.200
After all, “a picture is worth a thousand words.”

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.250
How many slides do you plan to use in your PowerPoint?

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.080
Not too many, just about 50.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.270
That’s a lot

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.290 
You should keep the number of slides to a minimum

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.200 
You don’t need to put everything you say on them 

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.190
Ok, I will cut down the number of slides 

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.000
for my presentation. 

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.230
I also need to enlarge the font size 

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.200
and change the style

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.250 
I think I included too many words

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:38.200
and images on a single slide

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.000
You should limit the amount of material on each slide

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:45.100 
The visual aid should be visible 

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.200
to the entire audience 

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.050
After finishing all the slides

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.050 
I will double check the spelling

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:55.030
and grammar for mistakes

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.280
Now that you have all the slides ready

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.080 
it’s crucial to run through them 

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.110
before the actual presentation

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:07.200
Yes. That’s called a “technical rehearsal,” right?

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.170
Right. Set up the audio and video equipment

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.200
and test them

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.000 
Get everything ready before the presentation

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.000 
Also, during the presentation

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.130 
you can check with the audience by asking

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.200
“Can everyone hear clearly?”

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:27.100 
or “Can you see the screen from the back row?”


00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.010
Should I introduce the visual aid to the audience

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.160
when they first see it?

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.180
Talk about the visual aid by pointing to the screen

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.080
“As you can see from this graph…”

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.290 
or “This chart gives you a breakdown of…”

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.020
Visual aids can really enhance the core message

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.150 
and help the audience understand the information better

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.070
Following the slides can help the presenter 

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.060
focus on the subject, too.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.240
Let me show you some pictures I’m putting on my slides

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.200
Those pictures are great

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.000
Now you’re making the best use of your visual aids

